## Metadata
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-01-11
Notes: A 13-wide diamond (the outline of Nos. 1 and 3) with a black cross in the centre (shown as _), lettered "CAN YOU SOLVE IT?" in the reprint. No credit, no number; the reprint's own headline, "A Puzzle For Mail and Breeze Boys and Girls", is not the World's and is not used as a Title. The solution prints ROAB for 15-16 "A son of Lot." (Moab); the grid follows the solution. Intro as printed in the reprint: "HERE is a cross-word puzzle. Can you solve it? Fill in the spaces in diagram with words which agree with the definitions, apportioning one letter to each square. For instance, 1-2 means to help; the word is aid. Can you find the rest?" Read by hand from the Farmers Mail and Breeze's reprint of 1914-02-14 (Kansas_Farmer_and_Mail_and_Breeze_1914_02_14_16.jpg), solution from the Milwaukee Sentinel's Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_01_18_83_key.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.
Numbering: across-first


